I decided to check out the new fork at un.nethack.nu - here's spoilers/
gripes/ideas in no real order.

Early game play as usual.  First difference I see is the SporkHack orc
variant of minetown.  I've always hated this, and I'm not the only
one.  It doesn't balance anything, and takes away a source of price-
ID, hardware, light source, and protection.  Get rid of it.

The artifact-naming ID loophole doesn't work, but misleads you by
slipping on any item of the class.  This is a really nasty trick.
"Oh, its not an amulet of strangle/sleep or a HoOA".  If the author
wants to nerf it, fine.  But do it honestly - saying "There is only
one Eye of the Aethiopica" would get the point across without abusing
the player.

Sokoban is the Slashem maps run thru the flip patch.  I like it - the
spoilers still work, but you have to mirror-think.  Can't really use
muscle memory to do the old levels any more.  At the end, you have
prizes in all 3 rooms, but BEWARE - if you pick one up, the other two
vanish.  I ended up with the booby prize this way - the amulet of life
saving, when I really wanted the BoH.

One level below Soko entrance was another upstairs which went up a few
normal levels to a mall-style level.  Smaller stores than Slashem, but
welcome anyway.  The shopkeepers here don't carry much money.  My dog
had eaten a chameleon and turned into a mastodon (!) by this time, and
I cleared this and minetown with a magic whistle.  Didn't end up with
enough money for full protection.

I found 3 magic lamps in the mines, and a fourth on the quest.  True
to the wiki, the chances of a wish were less, so I kept one for
permanent light, and got the wish on the last one I rubbed.  I had
Excalibur, so I wasn't too worried about traps.  Silver dragon scale
mail, please.  Doesn't exist in the game.  Check the wiki - no clue.
Download the source.  Only 3.5.1 available, and silver scale is
there.  Check the 3 ascension dumps on the host server.  OK,
reflecting dragon scale mail.  The djinni says he's not allowed to
gift magical items.  I don't know and can't find the names of any
other dragon scale mail, so shield of reflection.  Magical.  Cloak of
MR.  Magical.  Magic marker. BoH.  Nope.  Same with artifacts, rings,
wands, scrolls, and potions.  Wished for lembas just to have
something.  An athame might have been better.  Just don't bother, its
worth more as a light source.  Castle wand supposed to be non-
rechargable.  Fair enough.  When I got there, it was 1:0.  Had to
wrest it to get my cloak of MR.  I'm feeling very abused by now.
Thrones don't give wishes either.  Why doesn't the author just remove
wishes from the game entirely?

One-Eyed Sam's Black Market is supposed to be in the game, but I
searched everywhere for the portal and never found it.  Probably in
some undisclosed location.  No signals like you get in Slashem on
entering the level with the portal.

Dragons have different names, and their attack matches the kind of
scales you get, but the color is randomized, and there is no name
reference, meaning that you have no idea what a dragon is going to zap
you with until it happens and you can remember it or record it on a
list.

Potions - you're going to need a spreadsheet.  Alchemy is by color
mixing now - its like paint - a neat idea.  Can't brew smoky anymore,
but they're so useless it doesn't matter.  The cancelling/unihorn/
amethyst alchemy still works.  There are primary, secondary, and
tertiary (brown) colors in light and dark.  The problem with this is
the loads of new non-color potion description names - it makes the
total descriptions in the upper 30s for only 26 potions (not including
blood).   You end up with a lot of missing links in the alchemy.
Luckily for me, I had two full alchemy paths to ochre (gain level),
fruit juice was brown, and white was in the game.  Gain level was the
only thing worth alchemizing, and I brewed 31 of them with no
problem.  I would expect most games to have no meaningful alchemy
available - I think the author should get rid of the extra useless
descriptions to remedy this.

Gehennom is the Heck patch, and its interesting enough - like
SporkHack.  Still too much maze.  I was wandering thru looking for a
bag of holding and the entrance to Vlads when I see a Green R - a
disintegrator.  I put on conflict, and watched its new foes vanish -
don't want that touching me - zapped it with fire a few times, no
dice, so I teleported it away.  I have only seen one magic map scroll
and no magic markers the whole game, so I'm mazing thru, but the
disintegrator chews thru walls like an umber hulk.  Tele it 2 more
times, then get some network latency while moving thru.  The
disintegrator appears next to me.  "Your gloves vanish!"  WTF??  A
message check shows "The Excalibur dissolves!"  At +7!  If one more
arrow had gotten stuck in the queue, I would have dissolved too.  This
is the most out-of-balance monster I've ever seen - way too
overpowered.  If you're lucky enough to get a real wish, get a blessed
figurine of one.  I quit in disgust, but I was looking for a reason
anyway.

Nethack forks are needed, cause the DevTeam has abandoned the game,
but this one is no fun at all.  Not because its hard (I've ascended 10
Spork) but because its nasty and undocumanted.  Derek Ray has done it
right with Spork from the start.  I don't agree with everything he's
done, but he has taken care to communicate all his changes and keep a
solid design vision.  UnNetHack can learn a lot from Spork.  Until it
does, I'm done with it.

